Revision history for Log-Dispatch-Email-DKIM

0.001.0
	First release: a Log::Dispatch appender that DKIM signs its mail
	Signs only for the domain in From:, passing over anything else
	A missing or unreadable key warns and sends the message unsigned
	Refactored: private helpers enforced with Sub::Private, messages through i18n()
	Sender may carry a display name; envelope sender and signing domain use the bare address
	A line break in To, From or Subject can no longer add a header
	Key lookup no longer uses glob() and works without HOME in the environment
	A missing From or To loses the message quietly instead of croaking
	Signing and sending are done by Mail::Send::DKIM (0.004.0 or later)
	Settings come from the environment: DKIM_DOMAIN (the domain in the signature),
	DKIM_SELECTOR, DKIM_KEYFILE, DKIM_KEYDIR and DKIM_SENDMAIL (SENDMAIL is the fallback)
	Added an EXAMPLES section: a complete log4perl configuration
	Declared the core modules used (Scalar::Util, autodie, base, version) and raised
	the minimum Perl to 5.026
	The test key in t/dkim/ is a throwaway made for the tests; it signs nothing real
